{
  "scope": "CPU-only optional exact factoring of accumulated frequency-basis tensors. Preserve every modular ciphertext coefficient, key switch, scale, rounding step, approximation and precision gate. Default grouping remains disabled.",
  "implementation_commit": "d87a879",
  "replay_control_commit": "0cd703e",
  "algorithm": "For each shared first root, sum integer complex-weighted second roots modulo Q, then take one tensor with that first root. Bilinearity over Z_Q[X]/(X^N+1), with i represented by X^(N/2), preserves the original accumulated tensor before its sole relinearization and rescale. Direct-root terms remain linear contributions.",
  "unit_coverage": "N512 and N16384 compare grouped and ungrouped ciphertexts using both exact RNS and FFT tensor backends. Full noncanonical random masks/bodies and mixed signed real/imaginary weights cover ring wrap and frequency differences. Transparent sparse Tanh outputs pass independent function and remaining-square gates. Counted sparse Tanh uses4 tensor products versus16 and exactly one key switch in both accumulated policies.",
